=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data sources (web useTranslation + useChartPalette + useFormatting): the web
    chart is a leaf taking `data: MonthlyBucket[]` + `vehicleId` props (the parent
    cost-analysis page derives buckets via useCostAnalysisData and owns isLoading/
    refetch). Reproduced through the P1/S8 seam MonthlyCostChartSource→Model: each
    coalesced MonthlyCostUpdate carries the buckets + load status + connection +
    annotations + vehicleId. No HTTP in the view.
      • useChartPalette palette[0] -> TSChartPalette.color(at: 0) (area stroke +
        gradient + tooltip swatch).
      • useFormatting formatCurrency -> MonthlyCostFormatting seam; y-axis uses
        formatCurrency(v, 0) (web), tooltip/summary use 2 decimals.
  - Composition (web ChartContainer + AreaChart):
      • title "Monthly Cost Trend" + container aria "Monthly charging cost trend
        area chart" -> panel header + container accessibilityLabel.
      • AreaChart cost-vs-month (web `data.map(d => ({month, cost}))`, costGrad
        0.30→0.02 fill, palette[0] stroke) -> Chart { AreaMark(gradient) + LineMark }.
      • x tick `${p[1]}/${p[0].slice(2)}` -> MonthlyCostFormat.monthTickLabel
        (YYYY-MM→MM/YY); y tick formatCurrency(v,0) -> currency AxisValueLabel.
      • annotations{vehicleId,scope:'cost',chartId:'cost-monthly-trend'} +
        renderAnnotationLines -> dashed RuleMarks tinted to ANNOTATION_COLORS
        (milestone/maintenance/trip/issue/upgrade/custom), aligned to a plotted month.
      • selection -> ChartTooltip parity (month + Cost ($)).
    Scope note: the ChartContainer's CSV-export menu + screen-reader fallback table
    (dataColumns Month / Cost ($)) are atomic shared-component concerns (P4
    component-library bundle), out of scope here; their source i18n keys are still
    carried in the catalog for parity.
  - States (ALL rendered, each with a #if DEBUG preview + a model/phase unit test):
      loading (skeleton) · content (area + annotations) · empty (web "Not enough
      data" via ContentUnavailableView) · error (message + Retry) · stale (freshness
      chip + "cost history may be out of date" banner + one guarded auto-refresh) ·
      offline (cached area kept + "showing the last loaded cost history" banner +
      offline chip, no refetch).
  - i18n (P1/S10): web keys preserved verbatim — costAnalysis.charts.monthlyCost /
    .monthlyCost.aria / .col.month / .col.cost / .cost / .noData. Native chrome
    namespaced costAnalysis.charts.{live,stale,offline} + costAnalysis.charts.monthly.*
